WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:05.490
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan, and
today I'm revealing 14 hidden easter eggs,

00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:09.929
adorable call-backs to the first movie, and
cameos you missed in To All The Boys: P.S.

00:00:09.929 --> 00:00:10.929
I Still Love You.

00:00:10.929 --> 00:00:15.730
Plus, I'll be explaining the secret end-credits
teaser that sets up the third and final movie

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:16.789
in the trilogy.

00:00:16.789 --> 00:00:18.880
Spoilers ahead if you haven't seen the film
yet.

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:20.050
"Let's do this."

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:23.920
Remember how Lara Jean fell on her back in
a faint when Peter spoke to her about the

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:25.900
love letter she wrote him in the first movie?

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:30.480
Well, it seems like LJ has something of a
habit of falling down during meet-cutes as

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:34.460
she lands flat on her back once again when
she runs into John Ambrose for the first time

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:35.460
in the sequel.

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:38.780
Though this time it's a bowl of candy that
sends her crashing to the ground!

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:43.579
In those two moments, we see LJ literally
falling for Peter and John.

00:00:43.579 --> 00:00:47.780
And it seems pretty fitting that Lara Jean's
meet-cute with John mirrors her meet-cute

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:51.920
with Peter given that they all end up in a
love triangle together.

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:56.140
When Lara Jean wins the snow globe at the
fun fair with Peter, she asks him to watch

00:00:56.140 --> 00:01:00.559
as she tips it upside down and then back again,
showering the couple inside the globe with

00:01:00.559 --> 00:01:01.559
snow.

00:01:01.559 --> 00:01:05.720
What LJ doesn't realise is that this foreshadows
how her world will be turned upside down by

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:08.020
John Ambrose later in the movie.

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:11.170
Like the snow globe couple, she ends up kissing
John in the snow.

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:14.780
"It's a funny thing, this relationship stuff.

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:19.729
One moment, things are upside down, but then,
like magic, there's glitter everywhere.

00:01:19.729 --> 00:01:23.570
And once it all settles, you're right back
in the fairy tale again."

00:01:23.570 --> 00:01:28.420
As LJ unwittingly predicted, when her kiss
with John Ambrose didn't feel right, Peter

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:32.689
arrived to bring the glitter back and they
both end up with another sort of fairy tale

00:01:32.689 --> 00:01:33.689
ending.

00:01:33.689 --> 00:01:34.689
And talking of globes, there's an enormous
one at the aquarium which looks flipped upside

00:01:34.689 --> 00:01:35.689
down compared to the position we're often
used to seeing it in.

00:01:35.689 --> 00:01:36.689
This shot comes just before Lara Jean and
Peter break up officially and reflects their

00:01:36.689 --> 00:01:37.689
emotional state of feeling upside down.

00:01:37.689 --> 00:01:38.689
When Lara Jean and friends get together in
their old treehouse haunt, there are numerous

00:01:38.689 --> 00:01:40.579
memories from their childhood pinned on the
walls behind them.

00:01:40.579 --> 00:01:44.850
One of particular note is a drawing that's
reminiscent of a Harry Potter sorting hat,

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:49.350
a link back to how LJ and John Ambrose used
to read Harry Potter together in the treehouse.

00:01:49.350 --> 00:01:54.320
"You said you were House Hufflepuff, and that
was my house, too, and I thought maybe that

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:55.990
was a sign that we were meant to be."

00:01:55.990 --> 00:01:59.859
There's also a couple of pictures of a dog
in the treehouse, which could be Chris's rescue

00:01:59.859 --> 00:02:04.079
pup she mentioned earlier in the movie or
it could be a nod to the novels where Kitty

00:02:04.079 --> 00:02:06.220
had a dog named Jamie Fox-Pickle.

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:10.781
There was already a hat-tip to that family
dog from the book in the first movie when

00:02:10.781 --> 00:02:14.069
Kitty asked her father,
"Can we have a dog now?"

00:02:14.069 --> 00:02:16.200
"No, but that's a nice try."

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:20.230
If you're a fan of the To All The Boys book
trilogy, you were likely delighted to see

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:25.150
author Jenny Han pop up in the first movie
as a chaperone at Lucas and Lara Jean's school

00:02:25.150 --> 00:02:26.150
dance.

00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:30.840
This time she makes an appearance during the
Valentine's Day scene in the school cafeteria.

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:35.120
Just before the acapella group appears on
screen serenading a fellow student, you can

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:39.680
spot Jenny comforting a crying, likely lovelorn,
teenage girl.

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:44.620
As a producer on the To All The Boys movies,
Han has also been a major influence on Lara

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:49.840
Jean's on-screen style, collaborating closely
with the franchise's costume department.

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:53.349
And Jenny isn't the only member of the Han
family to show up on screen in P.S.

00:02:53.349 --> 00:02:54.500
I Still Love You.

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:58.909
In the Korean New Year scene, you can see
her real-life parents playing Lara Jean's

00:02:58.909 --> 00:02:59.909
grandparents.

00:02:59.909 --> 00:03:05.129
In fact, Han told the LA Times that she and
her mother even taught Lana Condor, Anna Cathcart,

00:03:05.129 --> 00:03:09.810
who plays Kitty, and John Corbett, who plays
their dad, 'how to properly greet their relatives'

00:03:09.810 --> 00:03:11.489
for the scene.

00:03:11.489 --> 00:03:12.489
P.S.

00:03:12.489 --> 00:03:15.960
I Still Love You continues in the first film's
tradition of referencing 80s coming-of-age

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:21.519
movies by kicking off with Lara Jean energetically
dancing to "Then He Kissed Me" by The Crystals

00:03:21.519 --> 00:03:24.880
in a tribute to the 1987 feature Adventures
in Babysitting.

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:30.670
In fact, LJ actually recreates many of the
key moments from the opening scene of that

00:03:30.670 --> 00:03:33.459
film, such as miming to the song in front
of her mirror;

00:03:33.459 --> 00:03:36.879
spinning across the room;
singing "I love you" to a portrait of her

00:03:36.879 --> 00:03:41.310
boyfriend before kissing it;
using her curtains to make a bride's veil;

00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:45.440
and then finally falling back on the bed and
tipping her head to face the camera.

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:49.800
Kitty, of course, jolts Lara Jean back to
life with a sharp reminder that:

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:51.329
"Seriously, Lara Jean?

00:03:51.329 --> 00:03:54.329
Now is not the time to be fantasizing about
living in an '80s movie."

00:03:54.329 --> 00:03:58.629
And that moment itself is a funny call-back
to how the 80s were such an important cultural

00:03:58.629 --> 00:04:00.620
reference for LJ in the first film.

00:04:00.620 --> 00:04:05.299
For example, when they formulated their fake
relationship rules, Lara Jean used the opening

00:04:05.299 --> 00:04:09.879
scene of the 1984 movie Sixteen Candles as
the basis for the rule that Peter was allowed

00:04:09.879 --> 00:04:15.069
to put his hand in her back pocket.

00:04:15.069 --> 00:04:19.299
It seems perfectly fitting that a franchise
based on a set of much-loved novels should

00:04:19.299 --> 00:04:22.090
do its bit to celebrate the joy of reading.

00:04:22.090 --> 00:04:26.740
In the school corridor when LJ and Peter are
discussing John Ambrose's letter, look carefully

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:30.720
at the background and there are a couple of
display boards with the words "Books Can Take

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:34.199
You Anywhere"
and "Reading Gives You Wings" together with

00:04:34.199 --> 00:04:38.770
a beautiful 3D display of butterflies bursting
out of a pair of books.

00:04:38.770 --> 00:04:42.860
When Lara Jean uses an ice cream sandwich
to demonstrate to Lucas just how much she

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:46.210
overthinks her relationship with Peter, it's
an amusing moment.

00:04:46.210 --> 00:04:48.830
"Has Peter shared an ice cream sandwich with
someone before?

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:49.830
Maybe it's me.

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:53.210
Maybe I'm the one who wants to do more than
just share an ice cream sandwich."

00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:57.500
But the choice of this particular snack is
also a deliberate easter egg to Jenny Han's

00:04:57.500 --> 00:04:58.500
novel.

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:02.830
In the book, when the group get together at
the treehouse, LJ packs a bag full of ice-cream

00:05:02.830 --> 00:05:07.081
sandwiches and Cheez Doodles, rather than
the cupcakes she bakes and pizza John Ambrose

00:05:07.081 --> 00:05:08.710
brings in the movie.

00:05:08.710 --> 00:05:12.840
And just like in the book where Peter takes
the last ice-cream sandwich, in the movie

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:15.080
he also nabs the last slice of pizza.

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:17.330
"Is he... is he still like he was in middle
school?"

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:18.500
"What does that mean?"

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:23.120
"At parties and stuff, he would always take
the last slice of pizza.

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:26.560
And then whenever you tried to call him out
on it, he'd be like, 'I'm an athlete.'"

00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:31.090
When Lara Jean reads her original letter to
John Ambrose, memories of the Halloween party

00:05:31.090 --> 00:05:33.340
she dressed up for come flooding back.

00:05:33.340 --> 00:05:35.140
"I felt so lame.

00:05:35.140 --> 00:05:36.979
Like I didn't fit in.

00:05:36.979 --> 00:05:39.650
And then, you walked in as a deviled egg.

00:05:39.650 --> 00:05:44.160
And I realized...
maybe I'm lame in a cool way."

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:48.890
Of course, the blue beret that young LJ wears
is part of her French toast costume, but it's

00:05:48.890 --> 00:05:54.130
also a lovely shout-out to the novel in which
Lara Jean has what she describes as a "charming

00:05:54.130 --> 00:05:56.030
and jaunty beret collection".

00:05:56.030 --> 00:06:00.940
When Peter first finds out he's in a potential
love triangle with LJ and John Ambrose, the

00:06:00.940 --> 00:06:03.270
moment perfectly reflects their situation.

00:06:03.270 --> 00:06:08.540
Not only are he and LJ in a biology class
at the time, but the teacher is talking about

00:06:08.540 --> 00:06:11.000
how octopuses have three hearts!

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:16.260
And, like in their love triangle, one of those
octopus hearts is about to get broken by Lara

00:06:16.260 --> 00:06:20.290
Jean who dissects it in front of a squeamish
Peter, foreshadowing their break-up later

00:06:20.290 --> 00:06:21.450
in the film.

00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:25.310
But that's not the only bit of foreshadowing
in this classroom scene because there's also

00:06:25.310 --> 00:06:29.479
a hint at the location where Peter and LJ's
relationship will come to an end:

00:06:29.479 --> 00:06:34.630
"The octopus is a mollusc and we will get
to see one of those during next week's visit

00:06:34.630 --> 00:06:35.930
to the Portland Aquarium."

00:06:35.930 --> 00:06:41.069
Oh, and if you think back to the first film,
it was also in front of a fish tank at a party

00:06:41.069 --> 00:06:46.069
that Gen and her friend nosily quizzed LJ
about her new relationship with Peter.

00:06:46.069 --> 00:06:48.870
"What do you wanna know?"

00:06:48.870 --> 00:06:49.870
"Everything.

00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:50.870
When?

00:06:50.870 --> 00:06:51.870
How?

00:06:51.870 --> 00:06:52.870
How far?

00:06:52.870 --> 00:06:53.870
H on B?

00:06:53.870 --> 00:06:54.870
H up and down on P?"

00:06:54.870 --> 00:06:57.889
And it was in the same spot that Lara Jean
and Peter took selfies to make Gen jealous

00:06:57.889 --> 00:07:00.280
of their fake relationship.

00:07:00.280 --> 00:07:05.020
The first movie had a mid-credits scene that
teased the return of John Ambrose in the sequel.

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:09.660
And To All The Boys 2 also has a little end-credits
tease for the third movie though it's very

00:07:09.660 --> 00:07:10.660
well hidden.

00:07:10.660 --> 00:07:15.289
The song that plays right at the end of the
credits is called Better By Myself.

00:07:15.289 --> 00:07:19.470
It's by the band Hey Violet who've said it's
about 'realizing that sometimes it's better

00:07:19.470 --> 00:07:24.170
to be on your own and learn how to love yourself
before you try to love anyone else or be with

00:07:24.170 --> 00:07:26.979
someone that doesn't put in the effort you
need them to.'

00:07:26.979 --> 00:07:31.069
If you've read Jenny's Han's novels, then
you'll know that Always And Forever, Lara

00:07:31.069 --> 00:07:35.360
Jean, which is the final book in the trilogy,
focuses on the complications that arise when

00:07:35.360 --> 00:07:39.289
LJ and Peter look to life after high school
and their plans for college.

00:07:39.289 --> 00:07:43.759
The end-credits song in this movie doesn't
necessarily mean LJ and Peter will break up

00:07:43.759 --> 00:07:48.830
for good, but it does hint that LJ may spend
some time by herself working out what's best

00:07:48.830 --> 00:07:50.210
for her in the long run.

00:07:50.210 --> 00:07:53.770
"I am trying to make sure you know how to
rev your own engine.

00:07:53.770 --> 00:07:55.599
Make sure you know how to look after you!"

00:07:55.599 --> 00:07:56.599
"Yeah, okay, I get it.

00:07:56.599 --> 00:07:57.599
I get it."

00:07:57.599 --> 00:08:00.729
The cast and crew already filmed To All The
Boys 3 straight after P.S.

00:08:00.729 --> 00:08:04.970
I Still Love You, and Lana Condor has said
its 'definitely the [franchise's] most mature

00:08:04.970 --> 00:08:06.060
movie'.

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:09.940
And in an interview with Entertainment Tonight,
she also revealed that in the third film,

00:08:09.940 --> 00:08:14.060
"[LJ] really starts to make decisions for
herself that might be unpopular but at the

00:08:14.060 --> 00:08:18.349
end of the day, as a young woman, you have
to protect your own heart and make the decisions

00:08:18.349 --> 00:08:21.750
that are truly right for you regardless of
the other people around you."

00:08:21.750 --> 00:08:26.480
On the separate note as to whether John Ambrose
will ever make a reappearance in Lara Jean's

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:29.490
life, actor Jordan Fisher is keeping his lips
sealed.

00:08:29.490 --> 00:08:34.410
However, Fisher, Anna Cathcart, Lana Condor,
and even Noah Centineo have all said that

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:39.340
they think that Peter is great for LJ's younger
years, while John is an endgame boyfriend

00:08:39.340 --> 00:08:40.340
or husband.

00:08:40.340 --> 00:08:45.000
There's certainly plenty of debate among fans
over whether Peter or John is the better partner

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:49.280
for Lara Jean, and I did a full breakdown
and discussion about whether LJ made the right

00:08:49.280 --> 00:08:51.940
decision in my Ending Explained video.

00:08:51.940 --> 00:08:55.780
Tap the screen here or follow the link in
the video description to watch that.

00:08:55.780 --> 00:08:58.700
Now, did you spot any other easter eggs in
the sequel?

00:08:58.700 --> 00:09:01.410
And what do you want to see happen in the
final film?

